From 86981a9d02c8af5d8a993985095c1e204c329319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duo2 <duo2@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:09:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] hexagonrpcd: answer the sns_registry interface, map
 /sys/devices/platform

While the SSC sensors process builds its registry from the json
configuration it calls back into the application processor for Android
system properties: interface "sns_registry", one method,
get_property(in string name, rout string value) (on Android the vendor's
libsns_registry_skel.so, property_get()). Without it the DSP gets an
invalid handle back, and hexagonrpcd exits on the next call.

Answer it from a "name=value" file, <root>/sensors/properties; an unknown
property is the empty string, like an unset Android property.

Some sns_reg_config files also read vendor attributes below
/sys/devices/platform (Microsoft's soc:surface_util/surface_product_id):
map that directory to <root>/sysfs-platform/.
---
 hexagonrpcd/interfaces.c                |   1 +
 hexagonrpcd/interfaces/sns_registry.def |  23 ++++
 hexagonrpcd/meson.build                 |   1 +
 hexagonrpcd/rpcd.c                      |  19 +++-
 hexagonrpcd/rpcd_builder.c              |  19 +++-
 hexagonrpcd/sns_registry.c              | 134 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hexagonrpcd/sns_registry.h              |  20 ++++
 7 files changed, 213 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hexagonrpcd/interfaces/sns_registry.def
 create mode 100644 hexagonrpcd/sns_registry.c
 create mode 100644 hexagonrpcd/sns_registry.h

